@startuml hoh-sequence
' One task from goal to closure. Plain PlantUML; no network includes.
title HoH - briefing, planning, one task through the three roles, and closure

actor Customer
participant "Telegram" as TG
participant "Supervisor\n(harness or model)" as S
control "HoH protocol and loop" as H
control "DAG scheduler" as SCH
participant "Worker\n(ACP / process / A2A)" as W
participant "Policy verifier\n(deterministic gate)" as DV
participant "Git gate\n(worktrees and commits)" as G
participant "Critic\n(external, read-only)" as EV
participant "Documentation gate" as D
database "State store and journal" as ST

group Briefing and role selection
  Customer -> S : Goal or project idea
  S -> Customer : Briefing questions while requirements are unclear
  S -> H : role-catalog - which agents and models are available
  S -> H : driver-catalog - the explicit transport contracts
  S -> Customer : Choose Supervisor, Worker, optional Critic, attempt bound

  opt Customer wants a role checked before committing to it
    Customer -> H : role-conformance for one exact selected role
    H -> H : Invoke the role in a disposable git repository
    H -> H : Verify the repository is still clean afterwards
    H --> Customer : Persist exact version, model and platform evidence,\nor fail closed
  end

  S -> H : ""project-plan --write --enqueue"" with the formal specification
  H -> H : Generate .hoh/role-profile.json from the brief
  H -> H : Resolve each driver explicitly;\nnever infer one from an agent's name
  H -> ST : Persist the queue and the profile
end

loop Until the roadmap is accepted or blocked
  H -> SCH : Compute ready tasks from dependency states
  SCH --> H : Ordered bounded batch, non-overlapping allowed_paths

  group Attempts, prepared in parallel
    H -> G : Create an isolated worktree for this attempt
    alt ACP or a dedicated edge driver
      H -> W : One constrained task over a bounded session
    else Generic stdin command
      H -> W : Constrained prompt on stdin
    else Declarative process profile
      H -> H : Write a temporary prompt file or stdin payload
      H -> W : One-shot command with the required safety and model arguments
    end
    W --> H : Filesystem changes, logs, metadata
    H -> G : Verify the attempt's HEAD still equals the starting commit
    H -> G : Collect the binary unified diff from the attempt worktree
  end

  note over H, G
    Integration below is serialized in the original batch order.
    A worker never commits, merges or pushes; only the Supervisor
    side of HoH moves the canonical repository.
  end note

  H -> DV : Check task scope, patch policy and verification commands
  alt Deterministic verification fails
    DV --> H : Blocking findings
    H --> S : Failed run evidence
    H -> ST : Append the failure and its evidence
  else A customer decision is required
    S -> TG : Clarification or approval request
    TG --> Customer : Message
    Customer --> S : Decision
  else Deterministic gates pass
    DV --> H : Accepted deterministic evidence
    H -> G : Apply the patch and create a supervisor-owned commit
    G --> H : Exact commit id and diff

    alt Critic enabled
      H -> H : Enter review_pending and export the v2 bundle
      alt An automatic Critic adapter is configured
        H -> EV : Immutable bundle over the configured transport\n(direct structured model, or a read-only bounded harness)
        EV --> H : Judgment fields
        H -> H : Inject canonical identity, hashes, timestamp and attestation
      else Manual Critic transport
        H --> EV : Versioned bundle: task, commit, diff digest, scope, checks
        EV --> H : A closed decision - approve, reject or escalate
      end

      alt Critic rejects
        H --> S : Immutable findings and a correction brief; state rework_required
        S -> H : review-rework confirms the exact correction instructions
        H -> W : The original task plus supervisor-confirmed correction context
      else Critic escalates
        H -> TG : Customer question with the available options
        H --> S : State escalated; the queue stops
      else Critic approves
        H --> S : Immutable approval evidence; the readiness gate clears
      end
    else Critic disabled
      H --> S : Deterministic evidence closes the task as done
    end
    H -> ST : Append run, commit, bundle and decision evidence
  end
end

group Closure
  S -> D : Final documentation and project audit
  D --> S : Audit result and the list of missing work
  alt Audit fails
    S -> H : Create remediation tasks
  else Audit passes
    S -> G : Final supervisor-owned commit
    S -> TG : Project ready notification
    TG --> Customer : Final readiness report
  end
end

note over ST
  Every arrow HoH handles also produces a redacted journal event:
  actor, recipient, time, task/run/correlation ids, content and any
  tool metadata the transport exposed. ACP notifications carry the
  agent's own tool calls; a generic CLI exposes only the invocation
  and its output, and HoH does not invent what an opaque worker
  never emitted.
end note

@enduml
